    "summary": "Silver pendant, overlay technique, depicting Long Haired Kachina. The Long Haired Kachina is made up of rain symbols: the beard is a storm pattern, the arm a rain cloud, the lower part of the body a wave/cloud/rain, the bottom of the pendant is an inverted rain cloud. The shape is a thin tapering rectangle with a stepped edge at the bottom and a loop soldered back on itself. The overlay is raised. The silver sheet underneath is oxidised and scored to create the hair effect. The makers mark is a face with a beard.",
